# A deliberate departure from `skillsbench-history`, which has no `.gitignore` and
# instead asks the author, in its README, to "double-check no `.env`, `.cache/`, or
# `__pycache__/` content is staged" before every commit. Running the three generator
# scripts in `scripts/` creates `scripts/__pycache__/`, so that manual check has a
# standing failure mode; this file removes it mechanically.
#
# Deliberately narrow. It ignores build noise and secrets, NOT results: everything in
# `results/`, `artifacts/`, `recipes/` and `reports/` is the point of the branch and
# must never be excluded by a pattern here.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.env
.env.*
.cache/
.DS_Store
